<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>tiltrotor_tailplane</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version='1.5'>model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
   <name>Umran Meryem Karabakal</name>
   <email>umranmeryem16@gmail.com</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Tri-tiltrotor VTOL with a conventional empennage. Two tilting rotors under the main
    wing and one on the tail boom carry the hover and the transition; behind the wing a
    horizontal stabiliser with two elevators sits under the rear rotor, and a fin
    carries a driven rudder. In forward flight all three rotors tilt to 90 deg, the
    wing lifts, the rear rotor pushes, and pitch and yaw pass to the tail surfaces.

    Pitch in hover is thrust differential between the wing pair and the rear rotor, as
    in the tiltrotor_2plus1 model, so PX4's control allocation needs no change.

    Reuses the wing, propeller and elevon meshes and the aerodynamic coefficients of the
    standard_vtol, tiltrotor and tiltrotor_2plus1 models, none of which are modified.
  </description>
</model>
